/** @page jni_compatguide JNI Module Compatibility Options

    @tableofcontents

    This module supports the following compatibility option: \c "compat-types" which, when enabled, will disable the
    following type conversions:
    - Java \c byte[] to \c binary; instead this will converted to \c list<int>
    - Java \c java.util.Map to \c hash; instead this will be converted directly

    The %Qore types declared for Java methods and fields do not depend on this option: a Java map whose key type is
    \c String is declared as a hash (see @ref jni_collection_types), but with \c "compat-types" the value is a Java
    object, which must not be assigned to a variable or member declared as a hash; Java lists are converted to %Qore
    lists in either case.

    This option can be set globally for all Program objects with
    <tt>set_module_option("jni", "compat-types", True)</tt> before the module is loaded (a value that is
    @ref False in a boolean context, such as @ref False or \c NULL, leaves it disabled) or
    locally for the current Program container with the \c set-compat-types module parse option like:
    <tt>%module-cmd(jni) set-compat-types true</tt> or <tt>%module-cmd(jni) set-compat-types false</tt> to
    override the global setting.
*/
